arby enemy units die.","Gains extended Frighten when <Lord of Thunder> is on the field."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.9,"stats":{"hp":4000,"atk":300,"def":100,"res":20,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2}},"shellsnap_newt":{"slug":"shellsnap_newt","name":"Shellsnap Newt","icon":"/enemies-icons/Shellsnap Newt.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Newts that dwell in the depths of the bamboo groves. Naturally timid, they carry around their own eggshells even after hatching, so that they may withdraw into them at any time.","abilities":["Curls up and stops attacking when your units are nearby, or if <Lord of Thunder> is on the field."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.75,"stats":{"hp":8000,"atk":350,"def":250,"res":20,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":4}},"guzzlemuff":{"slug":"guzzlemuff","name":"Guzzlemuff","icon":"/enemies-icons/Guzzlemuff.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Large beasts that dwell upon snowy mountains. They are huge, and their strong forelimbs are able to effortlessly grab smaller beasts—adult humans, even—before swallowing them whole in their enormous mouths. Houei has many tales involving them, mostly used to scare children.","abilities":["Eats adjacent enemies with Weight 2 or below, increasing the Attack Range of its next attack and dealing AoE damage."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":12000,"atk":550,"def":800,"res":20,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":4}},"rocksheller":{"slug":"rocksheller","name":"Rocksheller","icon":"/enemies-icons/Rocksheller.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Phy